$ signet --help
-- stdout --
signet is the command-line companion to the Signet developer identity
registry on Stellar/Soroban.

It links a local wallet to an on-chain handle, manages signing keys, and
talks to a Signet deployment (the default hosted one, or a self-hosted
instance) over its HTTP API.

Usage:
  signet [flags]
  signet [command]

Identity & linking:
  identity    Resolve the Stellar identity signet will sign with
  link        Attach this machine's deploy wallet to your Signet handle
  unlink      Detach this machine's deploy wallet from its Signet profile
  whoami      Show the identity, deploy key, and handle signet is configured as

Deployments:
  config      Inspect and update settings in the current context
  context     Manage named deployment contexts

Contracts:
  dev         Develop a contract against a fork of its deployment
  sandbox     Run a deployed contract's functions locally against forked state

Other:
  bug-report  Print a redacted bug report and a pre-filled issue link
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  doctor      Check the local environment signet depends on
  help        Help about any command
  version     Print the signet version

Flags:
      --context string         deployment context to use (overrides SIGNET_CONTEXT and the config file's current context)
  -h, --help                   help for signet
      --insecure               allow a plain-http deployment URL on a non-local host (signed challenges travel in cleartext; use only against a deployment you control)
      --json                   write a single JSON result to stdout instead of human-readable output (diagnostics go to stderr)
      --network string         Stellar network to talk to (overrides SIGNET_NETWORK, the context, and default "testnet")
      --sign-with-key string   identity to sign with, for non-interactive use (same value as STELLAR_SIGN_WITH_KEY; not remembered)
      --source string          identity to sign as (remembered in the config file for next time)
      --url string             Signet deployment URL (overrides SIGNET_URL, the config file, and the default)
  -v, --version                version for signet

Use "signet [command] --help" for more information about a command.
